ns require no artifact execution or reuse; rc.6 emits no claim, advances no committed downstream pin, and claims no hardened profile. No authoritative commit, push, tag, release, checksum, signature, attestation, or implementation pin was created.\n- EVIDENCE: new cycle-3 raw logs, manifest/legacy/lifecycle/safety audits, acceptance/rejection matrix, and outcome report are attached to the board under `TASK-260720-3ag6pi_cycle-3-*`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache mode-0000 capability rework closes Linux review\n- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the published CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The final unstaged product delta contains only `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD and no `uv.lock` remains.\n- CAPABILITY: inaccessible owned Linux directories are acquired through rooted `O_PATH | O_NOFOLLOW | O_DIRECTORY` references and changed with `fchmodat2(AT_EMPTY_PATH)`. Unsupported kernels or architectures fail closed with `cache_protection_unsupported`; no path-following chmod fallback is adopted.\n- FAILURE SAFETY: unlock now occurs before destination reservation. Original mode is restored and reservations are removed across fsync, reopen, rename, retry, unsupported-capability, and cleanup failures. Tests cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, inaccessible `0000`, exact restoration, and zero reservation leakage.\n- NATIVE MATRIX: a disposable Ubuntu 26.04 Linux 7.0/aarch64 Lima VM ran the exact focused suite with pytest 9.1.1 on Python 3.11.15, 3.12.13, 3.13.12, and 3.14.3. Each standalone gate exited 0 with 40 passed and no skips. The VM was stopped and deleted after evidence capture; Homebrew Lima 2.2.0 remains installed.\n- HOST GATES: exact post-scope macOS focused pytest exited 0 with 39 passed / 1 Linux-only skip; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 888 passed / 7 skipped; strict mypy passed 63 source files; task-scoped Ruff, compileall, diff hygiene, distribution build, and Twine metadata all exited 0.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_linux-capability-matrix-evidence.md` records exact commands, real exit codes, candidate hashes, readiness failures, package setup, and VM cleanup.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protocol v6 rc.6 workflow regeneration parity rework\n- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-3ag6pi` retained the exact curator-spec rc.6 source at `.temp/TASK-260720-3ag6pi/rework-cycle-3` and preserved every accepted product byte. The cycle-4 delta against reviewed product commit `ddb181ca3b8e243f212e90ff26fcabe2234fb669` is exactly `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`, and `tools/test_validate.py`; neither real nor disposable index was modified.\n- FINDING CLOSED: both CI and tagged-release deterministic-regeneration commands now include `release/1.0.0-rc.6.json`. A new executable assertion extracts the Makefile and workflow diff scopes, fixes the canonical three-path inventory, and requires exact parity, preventing another silent workflow/Makefile split.\n- NEGATIVE PROOF: the retained rc.6 metadata-drift fixture reproduced the old blind command at exit 0. The corrected command exited 1 and identified only the drifted rc.6 `created_at`; no package code ran.\n- GATES: `make validate` exited 0 with 42 schemas, 447 vector files, 60 Python tests, and Go tests. Two independent regenerations and all recursive/cmp comparisons exited 0; `make regenerate-check`, `go vet ./...`, uncached Go tests, Go formatting, and diff hygiene exited 0. Clean `make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.6` exited 0 at byte-identical product commit `ddb181ca…`; its clean-check was not weakened or spoofed.\n- SAFETY: no stage, commit, push, tag, release, conformance claim, checksum publication, signature, attestation, or implementation pin was created. Evidence and updated all-pass story/rejection matrix are attached as `TASK-260720-3ag6pi_cycle-4-*`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache identity-stable publication closes R3 race\n- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The unstaged product delta remains exactly `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD.\n- RACE CLOSED: publication now retains the rooted no-follow staged-directory descriptor across atomic rename and seals only that exact inode. If another publisher moves it during the private-mode seal window, the first publisher never seals or quarantines the replacement by logical name; it opens the selected live winner read-only and compares pinned canonical receipt and artifact bytes.\n- DETERMINISTIC PROOF: publisher A is paused after rename until publisher B exceeds the retry window, quarantines A, publishes and seals a different inode, and returns. Identical bytes yield B=`published`, A=`reused-winner`; different bytes yield B=`published`, A=`CacheConflictError`. Both schedules leave a protected live hit, a sealed quarantined loser, and empty staging.\n- NATIVE MATRIX: exact mounted hashes passed the full POSIX cache file on disposable Ubuntu 26.04 / Linux 7.0 / aarch64 with CPython 3.11.15, 3.12.13, 3.13.14, and 3.14.6; each standalone gate exited 0 with 42 passed and no skips. The VM was stopped and deleted.\n- HOST GATES: focused pytest exited 0 with 41 passed / 1 Linux-only skip; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 890 passed / 7 skipped; strict mypy passed 63 source files; task-scoped Ruff, compileall, diff hygiene, distribution build, and Twine metadata all exited 0.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_r3-identity-stable-publication-evidence.md` records exact commands, exit codes, candidate hashes, non-green setup diagnostics, and VM cleanup.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 cycle-5 native Windows worker diagnosis and closure\n- TESTER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` on preserved base/worktree commit `15860e3f309888845b9271a257fb95f7c2825b56`; no CocoaSkills product source or repository test file was edited by the tester.\n- LAUNCH ANCESTRY: the inherited 88-byte launch capability reached the child, but the Windows venv `python.exe` redirector made the executing interpreter a grandchild. Launching the already identity-bound base executable restored exact manager-parent/worker ancestry while retaining the fixed installed `csk.exe`, isolation flags, environment, and hidden mode.\n- LAUNCHER IDENTITY: distlib removes `.exe` from `sys.argv[0]` before `csk.cli.main`; fixed Windows-only suffix restoration recovers the bound launcher without consulting `PATH`, environment, package input, or user options.\n- IMPORT TCB: base CPython necessarily places `python_home` on `sys.path`. Admitting it without binding it would allow root-level code before worker proof, so the complete bounded Windows Python-home import tree is now identity-bound while disabled site-package directories remain excluded. Tester regressions first failed 2/2 (exit 1) on stale manager/worker root validation and omitted fixed `python314.zip`, then passed 2/2 (exit 0) after exact-root deserialization and fixed-slot archive binding.\n- NATIVE WINDOWS: the unchanged candidate-6 fixture exited 0 with 5 passed / 5 host-specific skips in 295.103 seconds; all three accepted variants built and the hidden-literal/runtime-image negatives passed. A separate tester-owned plain accepted gate exited 0 with 1 passed / 0 skipped in 63.33 seconds. The output was validated and never executed.\n- LOCAL GATES: focused driver pytest exited 0 with 118 passed / 1 platform skip; strict mypy exited 0 over 65 source files; compileall and tabnanny exited 0. Whole-module unit branch coverage measured 54%, so no 80% whole-file coverage claim is made.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcomes `TASK-260720-2g21eg_tester-windows-worker-diagnosis.md`, `TASK-260720-2g21eg_test_windows_python_home_identity.py`, `TASK-260720-2g21eg_cycle5-windows-python-home-producer.xml`, `TASK-260720-2g21eg_cycle5-windows-native-candidate6.xml`, and `TASK-260720-2g21eg_tester-windows-accepted.xml`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 compile-driver cycle-4 review finds an unbound interpreter runtime\n- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` cycle 4 on CocoaSkills base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`; the clean local main clone and live `origin/main` matched, both dependency handoffs were accepted, and the reviewed wheel matched the candidate `go_v1.py` and `cli.py` hashes. No CocoaSkills product or test file was modified.\n- RUNTIME-IMAGE FINDING: the installed macOS worker binds the 52 KB Python launcher but not the owner-writable 5.4 MB `Python.framework/.../Python` Mach-O image that `otool -L` proves actually executes it. That image is absent from the identity request/proof/post-exec set and direct retained watches; a native kqueue reproduction confirmed that watching only its containing directory does not detect an in-place child-content write. The claimed pre-launch, manager-owned-worker, and post-exec identity controls therefore remain open.\n- WINDOWS-VENV FINDING: the Windows path treats `<venv>/Scripts/python.exe`, `<venv>/Lib`, and the venv root as a complete private interpreter. A standard CPython Windows venv instead uses `venvlauncher.exe` plus the base installation selected by `pyvenv.cfg`, where the actual Python DLL and standard library remain. The current resolver either rejects the ordinary wheel-in-venv layout before launch or binds the wrong runtime while omitting executing base-runtime code.\n- GREEN GATES: focused pytest passed 295 / skipped 4; full pytest passed 968 / skipped 6; the standalone wheel-installed native macOS fixture passed 8; strict mypy passed 62 source files; diff, tabnanny, whitespace, and conflict-marker hygiene passed.\n- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Rework must bind the actual interpreter runtime/load components through every identity phase, resolve Windows base-runtime semantics securely, and add native runtime-mutation and Windows wheel-in-venv coverage. Evidence: `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-4.md` and its task-scoped JUnit outcomes.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Install transaction engine review finds a macOS canonicalization stampede\n- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-z2z795` run `RUN-260730-0c7fda` reviewed signed CocoaSkills HEAD `a5ec015c0b5b51149c81a679ce259920a3523374` plus the single unstaged Windows-test delta. No CocoaSkills source or test file was modified by the reviewer.\n- GREEN SCOPE: the repaired Windows permission regressions passed natively and under a forced one-bit Windows identity; a negative control proved both tests detect disabled foreign-mode rejection. The prior 14 lock-integrity regressions, 13 contract cases, focused 129-test suite, strict mypy 2.1/2.3, Ruff, and package build passed.\n- CONCURRENCY FINDING: full Python 3.14 pytest failed `test_repeated_concurrent_home_consumers_survive_release_handoffs` (`1 failed, 807 passed, 58 skipped`), and fresh-process stress reproduced it on iteration 4. A six-second faulthandler dump showed same-home consumer threads still rescanning directory entries in `_canonicalize_darwin_existing_path` before `_ExclusiveFileLock.__enter__` starts its configured timeout.\n- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Rework must bound or eliminate the same-home macOS canonicalization stampede, cover preparation in the acquisition deadline or otherwise bound total acquisition, and add deterministic preparation-interleaving coverage. Evidence: `TASK-260720-z2z795_review-verdict_RUN-260730-0c7fda.md`, validation ledger, and raw-log archive.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
